{# ===========================================================================
   Theme init. Must run BEFORE first paint, so it is a blocking, non-module
   inline script and it sits above the stylesheet links in the head.

   /src/js/main.js cannot do this job: type="module" is deferred by spec, so
   it runs after parse and can only correct the attribute after first paint,
   which is a visible flash of the wrong theme for anyone who chose night.

   The whole job is: read the stored preference, validate it against an
   allowlist, correct the attribute. Deliberately NOT here: no matchMedia
   / prefers-color-scheme (v2 is a manual toggle only, no system trigger),
   no clock, no write, no aria work (the toggle button is not parsed yet).

   try/catch because localStorage throws in Safari private mode and under some
   storage-partitioning settings. The catch leaves the server-rendered value
   from site.json in place, which is the correct degradation.

   The writer half lives in /src/js/theme.js (Phase 2). These two share only
   the storage key string.
   =========================================================================== #}
<script>
  (function () {
    try {
      var m = localStorage.getItem("tajima:mode");
      if (m === "day" || m === "night") document.documentElement.dataset.mode = m;
    } catch (e) {}
  })();
</script>
